# 98. Security Invariants

These rules must not be violated.

### INVARIANT 01

Authentication never implies authorization.

### INVARIANT 02

Frontend controls never constitute security.

### INVARIANT 03

Default authorization is deny.

### INVARIANT 04

Consequential actions require explicit authority.

### INVARIANT 05

AI recommendations never automatically become human authorization.

### INVARIANT 06

Every important state-changing operation is auditable.

### INVARIANT 07

Audit records cannot be casually rewritten.

### INVARIANT 08

Users cannot elevate their own privileges.

### INVARIANT 09

Tenant boundaries are enforced server-side.

### INVARIANT 10

Expired or revoked authorization cannot execute protected operations.

### INVARIANT 11

Sensitive information is not sent to external services without authorization.

### INVARIANT 12

Security uncertainty never results in silent privileged execution.

