# 103. OpenCode Security Implementation Contract

OpenCode must not invent:

```text
roles
permissions
authorization states
audit events
security boundaries
```

If implementation encounters an undefined security decision:

```text
STOP
→ identify ambiguity
→ consult architecture
→ resolve explicitly
→ implement
```

Do not silently choose a behavior.

---

# 104. Security Definition of Done

The security layer is complete only when the system can demonstrate:

```text
WHO
can access

WHAT
resource

WHY
through which permission

WHEN
under what session

UNDER WHICH AUTHORITY
for what action

WITH WHAT RESULT
and

WHO CAN PROVE IT
through the audit trail.
```

---

# 105. Final Security Principle

AEGIS must never operate on the assumption:

> "The user is probably authorized."

The system must know.

And when it cannot know:

> **It must not execute the consequential action.**

That is the security standard required for a serious biosecurity and pandemic-preparedness operational platform.
